<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Graubünden</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Grisons, Grigioni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Graubünden, known in French and English as the Grisons, is the largest and easternmost canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chur">Chur</a>. It grew from the Three Leagues, an alliance of the Grey League, the League of God's House and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-the-ten-jurisdictions">League of the Ten Jurisdictions</a>, which ruled the area as a free state from the 15th century. It became a Swiss canton in 1803 and is the only trilingual canton, using German, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romansh">Romansh</a> and Italian.</p></div>
